Ask Brenda Viola about her company's name and she'll first make sure you say it right.

"It's Vici," she says. "Vici in Latin means I conquer."

The name isn't decoration. Before she ran her own business, Viola spent years doing what so many professionals do: working 12- to 14-hour days for someone else and wearing what she calls "the golden handcuffs of corporate America." She was fine with that, she says, until one year made it impossible to keep going the same way.

"In 2021, within a series of months, I lost my mom, the love of my life, my dog, almost my home in a hurricane, and almost my life in a choking incident," she says. "Maybe I'm a hard head, but that's what it took to wake me up and say, 'Okay, are you living the life you want to live?'"

Today, through Vici Communications LLC, Viola is a keynote speaker, author, culture consultant and executive coach. She still works those long days. The difference, she says, is that now they're on her terms, doing what she believes she was meant to do: "which is actually just to encourage people."

